<hr id="hr21"><p id="p22">The launch of the Monologue Notes feature encapsulates the sort of change I’d like to see in the productivity app space. In the age of coding agents and LLMs, features alone are no longer enough to differentiate your product from a competitor: they <a href="https://x.com/linuz90/status/2048788309451665807" rel="noopener noreferrer">can copy you in a matter of days</a>. Instead, it’s paramount to differentiate your product on narrative, user experience, design (now more than ever, I appreciate a great, human-made, non-vibe-slop design), data portability, and integration with AI agents. Monologue has all of these, and that’s why it’s now my default dictation app everywhere.</p>
